Day-02 Linux File System

File Hierarchy System (FHS)
/bin - contain binary command for all users
/sbin - system binary command for all users (we don't need to create command just need to run those which are already in system)
/root - is the root directory for users
/boot - this directory contain all the file and requirement this for bootloader.
/var - this directory contain all the log files , user mailbox.
/dev - this directory contain the hardware information of system
/temp - is the directory that contain temperory file.
/proc - this contain the information about the process and system
/sys - contain information about device and drive.


