####  Linu Boot Process  ###
1. Hardware boot phase
2. Bootloader phase
3. Kernel phase

1. When the system is power on the BIOS check the hardware weather the hardware are working good or not.
2. Then the control is passed to bootloader which load the require code to boot the system.
3. Boatloader takes the part of RAM disk and load the code(initrd or initramf)
4. Then it load basic OS and specific hardware drivers then the control is passed to kernel.
5. Now the kernel uses the RAM disk to start the OS and load daemon and other program.
6. Then the kernel dismounts and distroy the RAM disk to be used for system memory.
7. At the last kernel initialize system and load systemd


First program when the system is booted is GRUB2 Grand Unified Bootloader.
GRUB
-responsible to choose which operating system to load when the system is boot.

IT work in 2 phases

1. Stage 1 - GRUB is simply store in Master Boot Record(MBR) for BIOS.
2. Stage 2 - Stage 1 just load the grub and send it to stage 2 where user can choose the operating system.

## GRUB2 configuration file are present in..
1. /boot/grub/grub.cfg - update-grub and shell scripts 
2. /etc/grub.d - GRUB scripts
3. /etc/default/grub  - GRUB menu settings. help for customization

Updating GRUB
1. update-grub
2. update-grub2
3. grub-mkconfig
4. grub2-mkconfig

Daemon - this are the other program that define how the system work. This are often configure when the system boots.

Systemctl control the daemon process(process name followed by 'd',) like ntpd, dhcpd, sshd
- systemctl start <process> or systemctl stop <process>
- example systemctl start ntpd

To check the status of process 
- systemctl status <process>
